comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:13.251Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: metadata, body, and collection caches now retain compatibility files plus at most four fingerprint-addressed variants. Alternating extension-enabled and --no-extensions invocations restores the matching prior envelope instead of reparsing the corpus; variant writes use the existing atomic store path and retention prunes older identities deterministically. Cache-context changes are reported as diagnostics rather than warning noise."
  "2026-08-03T18:41:18.751Z","harness:codex","Real-scale acceptance on this 2,000+ item tracker after the fix: list extension warm 0.392s; first no-extension context creation 4.275s; restoring extension variant 0.432s; restoring no-extension variant 0.346s. Alternating restored get stayed 0.440/0.348s, context 1.771/1.355s, and next 0.751/0.694s. Runtime retained three fingerprinted metadata/collection variants plus compatibility aliases, below the four-variant bound. The previous persistent 5s mutual eviction is gone; only the first unseen identity pays construction."
  "2026-08-03T19:16:51.392Z","harness:codex","Review-loop implementation: exclude compatibility aliases from the four-variant retention budget; repopulate the fingerprinted envelope memo after atomic writes; tolerate per-file stat races during best-effort pruning; compute pmRoot once; assert the exact four-variant boundary; and exercise a retained variant disappearing between enumeration and stat."
  "2026-08-03T19:30:43.775Z","harness:codex","Exact-head PR evidence (PR #884, c361624e2): every hosted required check passes, including static/typecheck/coverage/smokes/compat, Ubuntu/macOS/Windows runtime smoke, benchmarks, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, DeepScan, CodeFactor, Codecov, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, and Docs/Skills. The complete sandboxed local suite passes 428 files / 6,792 tests at exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; lint, zero-clone analysis, 100% docstring gates, contracts, and focused review regressions pass. All 12 CodeRabbit threads were individually replied to and reacted to; nine actionable findings were fixed in c361624e2 and all threads are resolved. The requested exact-head CodeRabbit rerun was included-review-rate-limited and the authenticated Greptile gate returned free_reviews_limit_reached; these are reviewer limitations, not clean-review claims."
  "2026-08-03T19:40:15.045Z","harness:codex","Merge and operational evidence: PR #884 merged to main as 657f8fa56a1e56c918095a58600c49188206e180; local main equals origin/main and the worktree is clean. No open PRs remain; GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning each report zero open alerts; pnpm audit reports no known vulnerabilities. Telemetry flush at 2026-08-03T19:36:53.267Z successfully drained four queued events, while subsequent status commands generated fresh self-observability rows. Live Sentry 14-day data shows no new issue attributable to this tranche; older unresolved PM-CLI-2S and PM-CLI-2Q remain independently tracked by open pm-4odf0c and pm-qyg51h. The sole immutable same-day tag/package remains v2026.8.3 / @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.3; the scheduled Auto Release already proved same-day no-op behavior after that release, so this post-tag merge is intentionally eligible for the next UTC daily release rather than creating or moving a duplicate same-day version."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:13.645Z","harness:codex","Acceptance is asserted by rebuild count and source reads rather than fragile wall-clock thresholds: the regression test alternates runtime identities, confirms the previous variant is reused without item rereads, and verifies the four-variant retention ceiling."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-03T18:40:14.068Z","harness:codex",A fingerprint inside a single cache envelope validates correctness but cannot provide stability when two valid contexts alternate. The fingerprint must participate in storage identity and retention must be bounded; compatibility aliases can coexist for older readers.
